input.body:
The Category-3 append, after the pattern (#790) and cross-file tree (#800) rounds: checks whose subject is a parsed document's fields become declarations.

New spec vocabulary (documents parsed once per scan, shared across the rule family; unparsable/absent documents assert nothing):
- `checkParsedFile` — where a field is present, require/forbid another field (converts `aws-sam/esbuild-dependency`, with two new gates: `someTrackedFileContains`, `exactlyOneTrackedFileMatches`);
- `equalParsedValues` — two parsed fields must be equal, first file selected by path+content probe (converts `cer/version-sync`);
- `forEachParsedEntry` — iterate a document's named entries filtered by field equality, forbid an array value (converts `aws-sam/cloudfront-authorization`);
- `checkKeyValueFile` — dotenv-style schema: file exists, KEY=value lines only, closed key set, every key declared (converts `cer/release-config`).

Deliberately kept as code: the firebase functions pair (a two-document join through the shared `functionsCodebases` lib), `aws-sam/handler-path` (derived comparison), `growth-config` (in-memory config with per-field prose), `cer/privacy-permission-alignment` (shares `requestedPermissions` with the work-scoped sibling — one extraction, one home), and `web-speech-no-window-api-in-service-worker` (needs a parsed-field→file-set feed, a possible follow-up).
